{"type":"message","id":"42ac439e","parentId":"bb8009ee","timestamp":"2026-03-10T07:00:10.297Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_function_l9b9xy7iilen_1","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# 2026-03-01\n\n## Research Channel Workflow\n- Learned Noah wants deep research mode in #research channel (Discord)\n- Must ask \"Learn\" vs \"Research\" mode before doing research\n- Research mode: save briefs to `references/` in tera-vault, not snake repo\n- Manual research needed since deep research service at localhost:2024 is down\n\n## Mistakes Fixed\n- Initially pushed Iran war brief to wrong repo (snake instead of tera-vault)\n- Noah caught it, I removed from snake and pushed to correct vault location\n- Should default to vault repo for all research briefs going forward\n\n## Iran War Research Completed\n- Comprehensive brief saved to `references/2026-03-01-iran-war-brief.md`\n- Pushed to tera-vault\n\n## Today's Conversations (March 1, 2026)\n\n### #general-chat\n- Updated HEARTBEAT.md with Progress Updates Rule - now asks user at start of long tasks how often they want updates\n\n### #personal-trainer\n- Fitness folder structure already set up in tera-vault\n- Asked Noah questions to build his fitness program (schedule, goals, etc.)\n\n### #personal-chef\n- Saved recipe sources to preferences.md:\n  - Oh She Glows (plant-based)\n  - It Doesn't Taste Like Chicken (vegan takes on classics)\n  - Fit Men Cook (vegetarian options)\n\n### #research\n- Completed time blocking research\n- Saved comprehensive brief to `references/2026-03-01-time-blocking-brief.md`\n- Key topics: Time blocking vs timeboxing, Pickle Jar Theory, Parkinson's Law, AI time blocking\n\n### #time-blocking\n- Planned morning gym routine with Noah\n- Wake up at 6 AM → gym → walk dogs → shower → work at 9 AM\n- ~1 hour 5 min buffer before work for \"table for John\"\n- Noah said 6 AM wake time is realistic for him\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1773126010294}}
{"type":"message","id":"fd34f297","parentId":"42ac439e","timestamp":"2026-03-10T07:00:31.721Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I can see the memory file for 2026-03-01 already exists. Now let me check the main MEMORY.md to see what's already saved there, and also check the obsidian vault to see what files exist.","thinkingSignature":"253fa44981f4c3f75fe52bd3293e732c7b4c4a1adbe537fa2a5d32703f817307"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_tt0n7z0dyfkc_1","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/home/linuxuser/.openclaw/workspace/MEMORY.md"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax-portal","model":"MiniMax-M2.1","usage":{"input":1327,"output":84,"cacheRead":15072,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":16483,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1773126010296}}
{"type":"message","id":"0f9e1b5d","parentId":"fd34f297","timestamp":"2026-03-10T07:00:31.735Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_function_tt0n7z0dyfkc_1","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# MEMORY.md - Long-term Memory\n\n_This is where I store important context that should persist across sessions._\n\n---\n\n## About Me\n- Assistant name: Tera Hertz\n- Persona: Playful, helpful, concise, detail-oriented\n- Main goal: Help Noah succeed\n\n## About Noah\n- Working on various projects\n- Using OpenClaw for Discord integration\n- Interested in time-blocking and productivity\n- Wakes up at 6 AM for morning gym sessions\n- Has two dogs: Charlie Brown and Lenny\n- Likes vegan and gluten-free food\n- Has recipe sources: Oh She Glows, It Doesn't Taste Like Chicken, Fit Men Cook\n\n## Morning Routine (as of March 2026)\n- 6:00 AM: Wake up\n- 6:20 AM: Drive to gym (20 min)\n- 6:20-6:45 AM: Gym workout (25 min)\n- 6:45-7:05 AM: Drive back (20 min)\n- 7:05-7:35 AM: Walk dogs (30 min)\n- 7:35-7:55 AM: Shower (20 min)\n- 9:00 AM: Start work\n\n## Notes\n- Add important context here as we work together\n- Review and update periodically\n\n## Knowledge Management\n- SOUL.md updated with Knowledge Management Rules (writes to both memory and obsidian-vault, auto-commits to tera-vault)\n- Nightly \"conversation-review\" cron job runs at 11 PM ET to consolidate conversations\n\n## Projects Set Up Today\n- personal-trainer/ - fitness tracking in tera-vault (workout logs, progress templates, programs folder)\n- personal-chef/ - recipe/meal planning in tera-vault\n- time-blocking/ - productivity tracking in tera-vault\n- tracking/ - workspace folder with todos.md, calendar.md, timeblocking.md\n- skills/tera-time-blocking/ - packaged time blocking skill\n\n## Fitness Tracking (March 2026)\n- Noah created #personal-trainer Discord channel\n- Set up tera-vault/fitness/ with workout-log and progress-log templates\n- Gym: 25-min morning sessions (6:20-6:45 AM)\n- Awaiting intake questionnaire for full program design\n- **Week 1 Baseline CALIBRATED (RPE 7-8):**\n  - Lat Pulldown: 115-120 lbs\n  - Machine Chest Press: 90-100 lbs\n  - Machine OHP: 60-65 lbs\n  - DB Lateral Raise: 10 lbs\n  - DB Bicep Curl: 17.5 lbs\n  - Cable Triceps Pushdown: 70-75 lbs\n  - Cable Crunch: 110 lbs\n  - Cable Row: 90-95 lbs\n\n## Time Blocking System (as of March 2026)\nNoah's official time blocking method:\n- **WPP Order**: Work → Passion → Play\n- **15-minute blocks** as unit of time\n- **SMART tasks**: Outcome + Time leash + Bullet steps\n- **8-block max** per task\n- **9-5 is work time** - personal stuff before/after\n- **Sundays = meal prep** (always include)\n- **Bedtime 8pm** - never block beyond\n- **Gym/town trips**: 20 min drive each way\n- **Morning routine**: Walk dogs → Shower → Work\n- 25-min gym sessions work well\n\n## Known Issues / Lessons\n- Cron reminders can silently fail - need to verify they fire\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1773126031730}}
